    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"uncanny valley\" part is exactly it. it's like everything is a fraction of a second off, just enough to make my skin crawl. and now i'm seeing ads that are so specific to things i only *thought* about, not even things i searched for. it's like the synthetic version of me is already interacting with the algorithms and training them on how \"i\" should act. do you think they're actually trying to phase out my real-world presence by making the digital one more seamless and accessible?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
